1. Basic but Tricky Array Questions
1. Find the maximum element in an array
Traverse once and keep updating max; O(n).

2. Find the minimum element in an array
Maintain running minimum; single pass.

3. Reverse an array
Use two pointers swapping from ends; O(n), in-place.

4. Check if array is sorted
Compare adjacent elements; break if order violated.

5. Find sum of all elements
Loop or stream sum; O(n).

2. Rotation & Position-Based Problems
6. Rotate array by K positions (right)
Reverse whole array, then parts; O(n), O(1) space.

7. Rotate array by K positions (left)
Reverse segments then whole array; O(n).

8. Find element at Kth position after rotations
Use (index + k) % n; avoid actual rotation.

9. Move all zeros to the end
Two-pointer compaction; maintain order.

10. Move all negative numbers to one side
Partition like quicksort; O(n).

3. Searching & Index-Based Questions
11. Find index of a given element
Linear or binary search if sorted.

12. Binary search implementation
Divide search space; O(log n).

13. Find first and last occurrence
Modified binary search for boundaries.

14. Find peak element
Binary search on slope; O(log n).

15. Find pivot in rotated sorted array
Detect inflection via binary search.

4. Duplicate & Missing Number Problems
16. Find duplicate element
HashSet or Floyd’s cycle detection.

17. Find missing number (1 to N)
Sum formula or XOR trick.

18. Find all duplicates
Use frequency map or index marking.

19. Find first repeating element
Track using set; return earliest repeat.

20. Find missing and repeating number
Math equations or XOR approach.

5. Subarray Problems (Very Important)
21. Maximum subarray sum (Kadane’s)
Track running sum; reset on negative.

22. Find subarray with given sum
Sliding window (positive) or hashmap.

23. Count subarrays with sum K
Prefix sum + hashmap.

24. Longest subarray with sum K
Store first occurrence of prefix sum.

25. Maximum product subarray
Track max and min due to negatives.

6. Two Pointer & Sliding Window Problems
26. Two sum problem
Hashmap for complement lookup.

27. Three sum problem
Sort + two pointers; O(n²).

28. Container with most water
Move smaller height pointer inward.

29. Longest substring without repeating
Sliding window + set/map.

30. Minimum window substring
Expand/shrink window using frequency map.

7. Sorting-Based Questions
31. Sort 0s, 1s, 2s
Dutch National Flag algorithm.

32. Merge two sorted arrays
Two pointers or extra buffer.

33. Find kth smallest element
Heap or quickselect.

34. Check if two arrays are equal
Sort or hashmap frequency.

35. Rearrange array alternately
Max-min pattern using extra space.

8. Advanced Pattern-Based Problems
36. Trapping rain water
Two pointers or prefix arrays.

37. Stock buy and sell
Track min price and max profit.

38. Find leaders in array
Traverse from right, track max.

39. Product of array except self
Prefix + suffix product arrays.

40. Majority element
Boyer-Moore voting algorithm.

9. Matrix (2D Array) Problems
41. Rotate matrix by 90 degrees
Transpose + reverse rows.

42. Spiral traversal
Layer-by-layer boundary traversal.

43. Search in sorted matrix
Start top-right; eliminate row/col.

44. Set matrix zeros
Use first row/column as markers.

45. Count islands
DFS/BFS traversal on grid.

10. Hard & Interview Favorite Problems
46. Median of two sorted arrays
Binary search partition.

47. Sliding window maximum
Deque for O(n) solution.

48. Longest consecutive sequence
HashSet for O(n).

49. Maximum XOR pair
Trie or bit manipulation.

50. Subarray with equal 0s and 1s
Convert 0 → -1 and use prefix sum.

11. Scenario-Based & Story Problems (Most Important for Senior Interviews)
51. You are building a logging system — find peak traffic window
Convert timestamps to array and use sliding window max.

52. E-commerce: find top K selling products
Use hashmap + heap for frequency tracking.

53. Payment system: detect duplicate transactions within 5 mins
Sort by time and use sliding window comparison.

54. Social media feed: show most recent unique posts
Use HashSet + reverse traversal.

55. Analytics: find longest stable metric period
Convert to longest subarray with condition.

56. Ride-sharing: maximize rides without overlap
Sort intervals and apply greedy selection.

57. Stock system: best time to buy/sell multiple times
Track increasing sequences (greedy).

58. Fraud detection: find unusual spikes
Use prefix sum or sliding window anomaly detection.

59. Gaming leaderboard: maintain top N players
Use min-heap of size N.

60. Notification system: batch events in fixed window
Group events using windowing technique.

